---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: the vault's client is locked and there is no terminal to ask its master
password on. Nothing was read.

The refusal is here rather than after the first mapping deliberately: a run
that prompted into the void would have decrypted safix's side of every
mapping first, and a run that treated a locked vault as an empty one would
report every mapping as one-sided and, in backup mode, write.

Run this where you can type, or unlock the client first and let safix use
the session it finds:

    bw unlock
